1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,480
Welcome to Before the Merge. This is

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:04,680
episode three, Before You Expand

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:05,360
Autonomia.

4
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:08,040
What should a small software team test

5
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:08,680
next?

6
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:11,040
Our evidence is current as of October

7
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,880
15th, 2026.

8
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,520
This presentation uses an AI generated

9
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:16,840
presenter and voice.

10
00:00:16,970 --> 00:00:19,369
The  first  episode  separated  workflow

11
00:00:19,369 --> 00:00:21,050
demonstrations  from  delivery

12
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:23,249
outcomes.  The  second  separated

13
00:00:23,249 --> 00:00:24,729
commercial  claims  from  measured

14
00:00:24,729 --> 00:00:25,890
evidence.

15
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:28,170
Our  final  argument  is  practical.

16
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:30,649
New  tools  create  options,  but  a

17
00:00:30,649 --> 00:00:32,930
decision  to  grant  more  autonomy

18
00:00:32,930 --> 00:00:34,249
should  depend  on  a  bounded

19
00:00:34,249 --> 00:00:36,810
evaluation  of  the  team's  own  work.

20
00:00:36,810 --> 00:00:38,530
The  evaluation  plan  in  this  video

21
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:40,810
is  our  proposal,  not  an  experiment

22
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:42,530
we  have  already  conducted.

23
00:00:42,851 --> 00:00:44,651
Three  written  sources  frame  that

24
00:00:44,651 --> 00:00:47,211
proposal.  First,  GitHub's  October

25
00:00:47,211 --> 00:00:50,011
13th  announcement,  Gemini  4  Argon

26
00:00:50,011 --> 00:00:52,090
in  GitHub  copilot,  states  that  the

27
00:00:52,090 --> 00:00:53,851
model  is  available  to  specified

28
00:00:53,851 --> 00:00:55,771
copilot  plans  and  can  be  selected

29
00:00:55,771 --> 00:00:57,410
in  the  model  picker.  That  is

30
00:00:57,410 --> 00:00:59,730
evidence  of  an  available  option.

31
00:00:59,730 --> 00:01:01,650
Availability  does  not  by  itself

32
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:03,730
demonstrate  faster  delivery,  fewer

33
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:06,371
defects  or  less  human  review.  We

34
00:01:06,371 --> 00:01:07,730
do  not  treat  the  announcement  as

35
00:01:07,730 --> 00:01:09,210
an  independent  measurement  of  those

36
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:10,051
outcomes.

37
00:01:10,251 --> 00:01:12,612
Second,  Cloud Flyers'  Birthday  Week

38
00:01:12,612 --> 00:01:15,811
2026  Roundup  reports  that  automated

39
00:01:15,811 --> 00:01:18,452
traffic  surpassed  human  activity

40
00:01:18,452 --> 00:01:20,092
and  describes  the  influence  of

41
00:01:20,092 --> 00:01:22,332
agent  driven  recommendations.

42
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:23,851
This  is  a  vendor's  account  of  a

43
00:01:23,851 --> 00:01:26,532
broader  agent  ecosystem.  It  helps

44
00:01:26,532 --> 00:01:28,572
explain  why  teams  face  more  agent

45
00:01:28,572 --> 00:01:30,732
related  choices,  but  the  passage

46
00:01:30,732 --> 00:01:32,372
retained  for  this  piece  does  not

47
00:01:32,372 --> 00:01:34,532
measure  coding  productivity.

48
00:01:34,532 --> 00:01:35,772
We  should  not  turn  a  statement

49
00:01:35,772 --> 00:01:37,532
about  internet  activity  into  a

50
00:01:37,532 --> 00:01:38,892
claim  about  a  software  team's

51
00:01:38,892 --> 00:01:39,972
performance.

52
00:01:39,973 --> 00:01:43,892
Third,  MeTR's  October  14th  article,

53
00:01:43,892 --> 00:01:45,653
Our  Approach  to  Working  with  AI

54
00:01:45,653 --> 00:01:47,892
Companies,  describes  its  goal  of

55
00:01:47,892 --> 00:01:49,933
producing  accurate,  timely,

56
00:01:49,933 --> 00:01:51,893
independent  evidence  about  loss  of

57
00:01:51,893 --> 00:01:54,173
control  risk.  It  emphasizes

58
00:01:54,173 --> 00:01:56,453
collecting  concrete  evidence  and

59
00:01:56,453 --> 00:01:58,573
publishing  findings  while  noting

60
00:01:58,573 --> 00:02:01,012
that  some  questions  remain  open.

61
00:02:01,012 --> 00:02:03,133
Its  subject  is  risk  assessment,

62
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:04,613
not  a  direct  evaluation  of  our

63
00:02:04,613 --> 00:02:06,533
development  team.  We  borrow  the

64
00:02:06,533 --> 00:02:08,652
principle  of  explicit  evidence

65
00:02:08,652 --> 00:02:10,012
while  keeping  that  difference  in

66
00:02:10,012 --> 00:02:11,253
scope  visible.

67
00:02:11,534 --> 00:02:13,014
Together,  the  three  sources

68
00:02:13,014 --> 00:02:15,334
distinguish  an  available  capability,

69
00:02:15,334 --> 00:02:17,494
an  ecosystem  narrative  and  an

70
00:02:17,494 --> 00:02:19,294
evaluation  principle.

71
00:02:19,294 --> 00:02:21,174
Our  contribution  is  to  translate

72
00:02:21,174 --> 00:02:22,454
those  distinctions  into  a

73
00:02:22,454 --> 00:02:24,694
reversible  decision  process.  The

74
00:02:24,694 --> 00:02:26,053
right  question  is  not  simply

75
00:02:26,053 --> 00:02:28,134
whether  a  new  model  is  impressive.

76
00:02:28,134 --> 00:02:29,894
It  is  whether  a  particular  use

77
00:02:29,894 --> 00:02:32,293
improves  an  outcome  we  care  about

78
00:02:32,293 --> 00:02:34,094
at  an  acceptable  cost  and  level

79
00:02:34,094 --> 00:02:34,974
of  risk.

80
00:02:39,535 --> 00:02:42,735
Step one is to choose a bounded task with

81
00:02:42,735 --> 00:02:44,895
observable acceptance criteria.

82
00:02:45,375 --> 00:02:47,015
Avoid starting with a change whose

83
00:02:47,015 --> 00:02:49,015
failure would be difficult to detect a

84
00:02:49,015 --> 00:02:49,655
reverse.

85
00:02:50,095 --> 00:02:52,455
State what the agent may do, what it may

86
00:02:52,455 --> 00:02:53,215
not do,

87
00:02:53,615 --> 00:02:55,775
and who remains responsible for approval.

88
00:02:55,824 --> 00:02:58,344
Step  two  is  to  define  a  comparison

89
00:02:58,344 --> 00:03:00,304
before  seeing  the  result.  Use

90
00:03:00,304 --> 00:03:02,103
similar  work  where  possible  and

91
00:03:02,103 --> 00:03:03,504
record  differences  that  make  the

92
00:03:03,504 --> 00:03:05,944
comparison  imperfect.  Count  time

93
00:03:05,944 --> 00:03:08,463
spent  specifying,  reviewing,  testing

94
00:03:08,463 --> 00:03:10,304
and  correcting,  not  just  time

95
00:03:10,304 --> 00:03:12,384
until  the  first  code  appears.  Keep

96
00:03:12,384 --> 00:03:13,863
tool  use  and  cost  visible  as

97
00:03:13,863 --> 00:03:14,384
well.

98
00:03:18,391 --> 00:03:21,030
Step  three  is  to  inspect  outcomes.

99
00:03:21,030 --> 00:03:22,391
Did  the  change  satisfy  the

100
00:03:22,391 --> 00:03:25,111
intended  behavior?  What  defects  or

101
00:03:25,111 --> 00:03:27,151
rework  appeared?  Did  reviewers

102
00:03:27,151 --> 00:03:28,511
understand  the  change  well  enough

103
00:03:28,511 --> 00:03:30,591
to  maintain  it?  A  fast  first

104
00:03:30,591 --> 00:03:32,071
draft  that  creates  substantial

105
00:03:32,071 --> 00:03:33,790
laterwork  may  not  be  a  delivery

106
00:03:33,790 --> 00:03:34,711
improvement.

107
00:03:42,271 --> 00:03:44,432
Finally,  decide  in  advance  what

108
00:03:44,432 --> 00:03:46,871
would  justify  expanding,  repeating

109
00:03:46,871 --> 00:03:49,232
or  stopping  the  pilot.  A  positive

110
00:03:49,232 --> 00:03:50,832
result  on  one  task  supports

111
00:03:50,832 --> 00:03:52,952
another  bounded  test,  not

112
00:03:52,952 --> 00:03:55,272
unrestricted  autonomy.  A  negative

113
00:03:55,272 --> 00:03:57,152
result  can  reveal  a  poor  task

114
00:03:57,152 --> 00:03:59,191
fit,  rather  than  prove  every  agent

115
00:03:59,191 --> 00:04:00,312
is  ineffective.

116
00:04:06,313 --> 00:04:08,152
Our  evidence  cannot  supply  a

117
00:04:08,152 --> 00:04:10,312
universal  threshold  or  guarantee  a

118
00:04:10,312 --> 00:04:12,713
benefit.  Small  samples,  task

119
00:04:12,713 --> 00:04:14,953
differences  and  evaluator  judgment

120
00:04:14,953 --> 00:04:16,752
remain  limitations.

121
00:04:16,752 --> 00:04:18,592
But  a  transparent  pilot  makes  the

122
00:04:18,592 --> 00:04:21,233
next  decision  inspectable.  That  is

123
00:04:21,233 --> 00:04:23,073
the  series  takeaway.  Define  the

124
00:04:23,073 --> 00:04:25,713
job,  examine  the  claim  and  measure

125
00:04:25,713 --> 00:04:27,393
the  outcome  before  expanding

126
00:04:27,393 --> 00:04:28,353
autonomy.

